    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from an 8% ULCC baseline, the analysis applies downward pressure from concrete liquidity and merger progress, while upward pressure comes from Altman Z-score distress, debt-maturities refinancing risk, and sector distress signals. The net result is a modest, non-negligible probability of bankruptcy within the window, calibrated to a central estimate around 12% with an 8–20% uncertainty band. Calibration acknowledges that large external events (e.g., a failed merger or a renewed liquidity squeeze) could shift the probability higher, while successful close and stable macro conditions could pull it lower."
